  "narrative": "I used the signed convention: for direction -1 mean differences, a positive estimate supports stronger dependency in the exposed group because more negative CRISPR dependency scores indicate stronger dependency; for direction +1 mean differences, a positive estimate supports weaker dependency in the exposed group. For interactions, positive signed evidence supports the registered interaction direction. I treated an absolute dependency-score separation of about 0.1 as a practical scientific benchmark, together with interval exclusion of zero, cell counts, and convergence across related contexts.\n\nH195 is a strong, precise PTEN-STAT3 stratum estimate: R172 is +0.211 with 95% CI +0.152 to +0.269 in IFN-gamma-low cells. The point and lower bound exceed the 0.1 benchmark, so I accept and close it as evidence that PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency even outside the inflammatory IFN-high context. H196 is similarly strong: R173 is +0.269 with CI +0.192 to +0.346 in the lower-half Cas9 stratum. This supports robustness to screen-quality selection, so I accept and close it.\n\nThe two MTAP-attenuation interaction probes are suggestive but not certified. H191 gives R170 +0.282 with CI -0.028 to +0.592 and smallest cell 33. H190 gives R171 +0.232 with CI -0.077 to +0.541 and smallest cell 34. Both point estimates exceed the 0.1 benchmark and are directionally consistent with attenuation, but the intervals include zero and the focal cells are small. I therefore leave the scientific status unresolved but close these direct probes; the supplied dataset does not robustly certify MTAP attenuation of the TP53-loss weaker-USP7 association.\n\nH172 tests PTEN-STAT3 by Avana-library interaction. R174 is +0.196, which is larger than the practical benchmark and excludes zero, but the lower bound is only +0.033 and the non-Avana focal cell is small (27 exposed). This makes the library-context difference plausible but imprecise, and it could partly reflect technical/library imbalance rather than a stable biological context. I keep the claim unresolved and close further follow-up on this specific library interaction. The non-Avana direct stratum remains underpowered, so I do not convert the library result into a precise context claim.\n\nThe TMED10 probes are all specific but negative. H175 PTEN-TMED10 R175 is -0.012 with CI -0.036 to +0.011. H51 KEAP1-TMED10 R176 is -0.001 with CI -0.021 to +0.018. H52 MSI-TMED10 R177 is +0.016 with CI -0.016 to +0.048. H33 ERBB2-TMED10 R178 is +0.001 with CI -0.027 to +0.030. H121 EGFR-TMED10 R179 is +0.004 with CI -0.026 to +0.034. These are far below the 0.1 benchmark and do not support meaningful TMED10 dependency associations in the tested contexts. I reject them.\n\nMYC probes are also null. H124 MYC-MDM2 overall R180 is +0.008 with CI -0.021 to +0.036. H203 MYC-KIF18A within high 8q24 copy-number context R181 is +0.002 with CI -0.023 to +0.026. Neither supports a scientifically meaningful MYC association, and the 8q24 context does not rescue the previous null KIF18A signal. I reject both.\n\nNo independent validation was requested because no new validation requests remain, and the new accepted PTEN-STAT3 strata are already within an extensively converged accepted axis. All accepted conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations, not causal or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Round-14 appraise update. Signed convention retained. Validation requests are exhausted, so future allocation is discovery-only. Accepted new PTEN-STAT3 strata: H195 IFN-low, R172 +0.211 CI +0.152 to +0.269; H196 lower-half Cas9, R173 +0.269 CI +0.192 to +0.346. These support PTEN-loss-associated stronger STAT3 dependency outside IFN-high and lower Cas9-quality contexts, with lower bounds above the 0.1 benchmark. MTAP attenuation of TP53-USP7 remains unresolved: H191 R170 +0.282 CI -0.028 to +0.592; H190 R171 +0.232 CI -0.077 to +0.541. Points are large but intervals include zero and focal cells are small; close direct probes. H172 Avana-library interaction R174 +0.196 CI +0.033 to +0.358 is plausible but imprecise and small-cell sensitive; leave unresolved and close. Reject all new TMED10 specificity probes: PTEN, KEAP1, MSI, ERBB2, EGFR. Reject MYC-MDM2 and MYC-KIF18A high-8q24. The accepted supplied-dataset axes remain MSI-high with stronger WRN; KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2; SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2; TP53 loss with weaker USP7; CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2; PTEN loss with stronger STAT3. PTEN-STAT3 is broad across TP53 strata, library context, Cas9 strata, IFN strata, driver-negative contexts, and other molecular contexts, but some context interactions remain imprecise. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset only."
}

