  "narrative": "No assessments are due and voluntary independent validation is exhausted, so this explore stage registers targeted follow-up comparisons for the main unresolved scientific question: whether MTAP loss attenuates the accepted TP53-loss-associated weaker USP7 dependency, or whether this apparent attenuation is an artifact of technical screen quality, subgroup selection, or genomic co-deletion context. I retain the signed convention: for direction -1 mean differences, a positive signed estimate supports stronger USP7 dependency in the exposed/focal group because more negative CRISPR dependency scores indicate stronger dependency; for a direction -1 interaction, a positive signed estimate supports a raw negative interaction. For USP7, I use an approximate absolute dependency-score separation near 0.1 as a practical benchmark together with interval exclusion of zero and cell-size validity. The first proposal directly estimates MTAP-loss versus MTAP-intact USP7 dependency among TP53-loss cells in higher screen_roc_auc screens. Expected direction is negative raw, or positive signed under direction -1: MTAP-loss cells should show relatively stronger USP7 dependency than MTAP-intact TP53-loss cells if MTAP loss partially offsets TP53-loss-associated USP7 hypo-dependency, especially when technical screen discrimination is higher. The second proposal estimates the same direct MTAP contrast in lower screen_roc_auc screens as a technical-quality complement; a similar positive signed effect would make the attenuation less likely to be confined to selected high-quality screens, whereas a null or materially smaller effect would suggest the apparent MTAP signal may depend on screen-quality stratification or noise. The third proposal directly estimates the TP53-loss effect interaction with MTAP loss within higher screen_roc_auc screens. The raw expected interaction is negative, so under direction -1 positive signed evidence supports attenuation: TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency is smaller in MTAP-loss cells than in MTAP-intact complement cells. The fourth and fifth proposals test a genomic confounding alternative. MTAP and CDKN2A are genomically linked, and CDKN2A-loss has an independent accepted axis toward stronger MDM2 dependency. If CDKN2A-loss itself mimics the MTAP-loss effect among TP53-loss cells, positive signed evidence for stronger USP7 dependency would support 9p21 co-deletion confounding of the MTAP attenuation signal; if CDKN2A-loss has no comparable effect, especially in higher-quality screens, the attenuation pattern is more likely to reflect MTAP-specific context rather than generic co-deletion. These comparisons remain associations in the supplied lung-like dataset and do not establish causality, mechanism, clinical actionability, or external generalizability. Some comparisons may fail the 20-observation-per-cell rule, and all interpretations should remain cautious about multiple testing and subgroup selection.",
  "research_notes": "Validation requests are exhausted. The accepted major axes are MSI-high stronger WRN, KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2, SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2, TP53-loss weaker USP7, CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2, and PTEN-loss stronger STAT3. The main unresolved issue is MTAP-loss attenuation of TP53-loss-associated USP7 hypo-dependency. Current registered MTAP probes include overall direct TP53-loss stratum effect H216, lower-Cas9 stratum H217, Avana stratum H166, high-Cas9 stratum H192, and imprecise interaction probes. This explore stage adds focused resolution probes: MTAP direct effect split by screen_roc_auc, TP53-MTAP attenuation interaction in high screen_roc_auc, and CDKN2A-loss mimic within TP53-loss overall and in high screen_roc_auc. Prioritize these in later analyze unless higher-priority untested claims appear. Interpret accepted context-specific results as robustness checks of the same broad axes, not independent replications. If CDKN2A-loss within TP53-loss shows a comparable effect, downgrade confidence in MTAP specificity because 9p21 co-deletion could confound the attenuation signal. If high screen_roc_auc direct and interaction probes remain imprecise, keep the MTAP attenuation hypothesis unresolved rather than treating the small positive H216 estimate as a scientifically meaningful modifier effect."
