  "narrative": "I assessed every newly delivered discovery result using the signed convention: each estimate and interval is already oriented to the registered hypothesis direction. Acceptance required valid comparison cells, a 95% Welch interval excluding zero in the claimed direction, and a dependency-score separation large enough to be scientifically meaningful on this continuous CRISPR dependency scale. \n\nThe clean TP53-loss/USP7 baseline remains robust. H277, testing TP53 loss among MTAP-intact/CDKN2A-intact cells, gave +0.423 (CI +0.335 to +0.511) for weaker USP7 dependency with TP53 loss. This is a large separation and supports the accepted TP53-loss/USP7 axis in a more genetically restricted context. H275 similarly showed a substantial TP53-loss effect within 9p21-low copy-number cells, +0.385 (CI +0.244 to +0.526), so TP53-loss-associated weaker USP7 dependency is not eliminated in that structural subgroup. However, H276 specifically tested whether the TP53-loss effect is attenuated in 9p21-low versus the remainder; the signed attenuation estimate was only +0.014 (CI -0.149 to +0.177). This rejects a practical 9p21-low structural explanation for the MTAP attenuation hypothesis.\n\nMTAP-specific attenuation of TP53-loss-associated weaker USP7 dependency remains unresolved. H273, the CDKN2A-intact TP53-loss by MTAP-loss interaction, gave +0.139 (CI -0.078 to +0.355), compatible with attenuation under the signed direction but not statistically or practically established. H274, the direct MTAP-loss contrast among TP53-loss/CDKN2A-intact/Avana cells, gave +0.220 (CI -0.061 to +0.502); this is suggestive of MTAP-loss stronger USP7 dependency or attenuation, but the interval includes zero. H258, a broader Avana-restricted MTAP-loss contrast within TP53-loss cells, gave +0.167 (CI -0.036 to +0.370), again imprecise. I keep the more targeted H273 and H274 active, defer the less specific H258, and do not accept MTAP attenuation as a separate supported claim.\n\nMTA